ase64 PNG, `mimeType` `image/png`) then a text block, the line without `png`, `isError` false; a refused shot one text block with `isError` true — a result that holds an image bounded at 1,048,576 bytes by its whole written form, a text-only one by its text, and runs an instance verb's tool call on the one instance it holds in process, `start` · `status` · `stop` and `help` answered by the server — `help` with the same line `escher-session help` writes, a session held or not — booted through the same boot `main` hands to the command line; it echoes a request's admitted `id`, and a result carries what the ratified crossing carries; its end writes nothing on stdout — exit 0 on `Ok`, exit 3 with the error's fixed message on stderr on `Err` (packages/escher-driver/src/cli.rs:40-42; packages/escher-driver/src/cli.rs:160-165; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:44-112; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp/listing.rs:28-48; packages/escher-driver/src/mcp/listing.rs:61-110); `start` checks its recording directory itself before it spawns, then spawns the same binary in its host role, `serve <task> --session <dir> [--record <dir>]` (in that order, passing `--record` to the host), its three streams closed, and that host ends with nothing written and exit 0 after a stop or its idle expiry and exits 3 on a session error; the host's stderr log lines carry `service.name=seven_guis`; unix only in 0.1.0. Since 2026-10-19-session-recording `--record <dir>`, taken at most once on `start`, the host role and the `mcp` role, keeps the session as one owner-only replayable check — `check-{n}.json` (`0600`, never replacing a file) in a `0700` directory whose parent must exist, never removed by escher, holding the calls and no screen reading (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-19: F1 A · F2 B) — a directory open to its group or others refused as the session error `record-dir-not-private` (exit 3, `start` spawning nothing), and a recording that ends answering the session error `recording-failed` (exit 